Subject: fix(server): report completion after waking remote closed agents

A prompt sent to a closed agent on another host is queued there (two quiet
seconds) before it resumes the agent. The caller daemon opens its finish
observation as soon as the remote acknowledges the queued prompt, so its
first refresh reads the old "closed" snapshot, waitForFinish(100) times out
behind the queue, and the code re-fetched that same closed snapshot and fed
it to the handler as terminal. The subscription delivered "was closed" and
was consumed before the resumed turn ran, so no "finished" ever arrived.
On a timed-out wait, report nothing (keeping a permission_resolved
checkpoint); the outcome comes from the dispatch-aware wait or a later
turn_completed event.

Issue: remote finish notifications lost after remote reboot (2026-11-14)
Applies-To: Paseo 0.15.2 resources/app.asar
Upstream-Status: backport of getpaseo/paseo 5062d5ee9 (#8575), in v0.16.0-beta.1
Drop-When: Paseo >= 0.16.0

--- a/node_modules/@getpaseo/server/dist/server/server/agent/host-operations/index.js
+++ b/node_modules/@getpaseo/server/dist/server/server/agent/host-operations/index.js
@@ -334,14 +334,17 @@
                     // A new turn may start between the snapshot and the current-response read.
                     // Bound that wait and refresh state instead of attributing the old event to it.
                     const current = await client.waitForFinish(agentId, 100);
-                    if (current.status === "timeout")
-                        snapshot = (await client.fetchAgent(agentId))?.agent ?? null;
-                    else {
-                        if (!current.final && current.error && current.error !== `Agent not found: ${agentId}`)
-                            throw new Error(current.error);
-                        snapshot = current.final;
-                        lastMessage = current.lastMessage;
+                    if (current.status === "timeout") {
+                        // Queued delivery can leave a closed/error snapshot visible before the new turn.
+                        // A timed-out wait has not established an outcome for that queued work.
+                        if (event?.type === "permission_resolved")
+                            handler(snapshot, event);
+                        return;
                     }
+                    if (!current.final && current.error && current.error !== `Agent not found: ${agentId}`)
+                        throw new Error(current.error);
+                    snapshot = current.final;
+                    lastMessage = current.lastMessage;
                 }
                 handler(snapshot, event, lastMessage);
             };
